102 - Unto the Hills
 / 
Key: F
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 102
Topic: God the Father - 

Verse 1:
[F]Unto [C7/E]the hills [Am]around [Dm]shall [F]I [C]lift [G7/F]up [Am]my [F]longing [Dm]eyes?
[Am]O [C7/Bb]whence [Bb]for me [F]shall [C]my salvation [Dm/F]come, from [Gm/D]whence [Am]arise?
[Am/E]From [F]God the [Gm/D]Lord [C7/Bb]doth come [Am]my [Dm]certain [Gm]aid,
[F/C]From God [C7/Bb]the [F]Lord, who [Gm]heav’n and earth [C/G]hath [F]made.

Verse 2:
[F]He [C]will [C7/E]not [Am]suffer [F]that [G7/F]thy [Am]foot [C7]be [Dm]moved;
[Am]safe [Bb]shalt [C/G]Thou [Dm/F]be
[Am]No [C7/Bb]careless [C]slumber shall [Gm]His [Dm/F]eyelids [Am]close,
[Am/E]who [Gm/D]keepeth [Dm]thee.
[Am/E]Behold [F]our [Gm/D]God, [Edim]the [C7/Bb]Lord, [Am]He [Dm]slumbereth [Gm]ne'er,
[F/C]Who keepeth Israel [Gm]in His holy [F]care.

Verse 3:
[F]Jehovah [C7/E]is [Am]Himself [Dm]thy keeper [G7/F]true, thy [Am]changeless [Dm]shade.
[Am]Jehovah [Bb]thy [F]defense [C/G]on thy [Gm]right [Dm/F]hand Himself [Am]hath made
[Am/E]And [F]thee no [Gm/D]sun [C7/Bb]by day [Am]shall [Dm]ever [Gm]smite,
[F/C]No moon [C7/Bb]shall [F]harm thee [Gm]in the silent [F]night.

Verse 4:
[F]From [C]every [C7/E]evil [Dm]shall He [F]keep [C]thy [G7/F]soul, [Am]from [F]every [Dm]sin;
[Am]Jehovah [Bb]shall [F]preserve [C/G]thy going [Gm]out, [Dm/F]thy coming [Am]in.
[Am/E]Above [F]thee [Edim]watching, [Am]He, [Dm]whom [C7]adore,
[F/C]Shall keep [C7/Bb]thee [F]henceforth, [Gm]yea, forevermore.
